## Theme palettes
Palette names (Catppuccin, Nord, Gruvbox, Tokyo Night, Rosé Pine, Kanagawa,
Everforest, Flexoki, ...) are used with attribution to their respective
authors; the palettes are MIT-licensed by their upstream projects.

## Third-party application icons (applications/icons)
The icons under applications/icons are the trademarks and logos of their
respective owners (Discord, WhatsApp, Zoom, Docker, Battle.net, X, YouTube,
Google, Basecamp/HEY, ...). Agentarchy neither claims them nor licenses them;
they are shipped only to identify the corresponding launcher in a menu, which is
nominative use. They are audited alongside the wallpapers before the first
public push, and any icon whose terms do not permit redistribution is replaced
with a generic one.

## Wallpapers (themes/*/backgrounds)
Agentarchy ships no wallpaper it did not make. The 68 images inherited from
upstream were removed on 2026-08-23: none of them carried a licence, and upstream
never asked contributors for one (see docs/asset-audit-findings.md for the
evidence and docs/asset-audit.md for the file-by-file trail). Every theme instead
ships one background rendered from its own colors.toml by
bin/oal-dev-make-wallpapers, which is part of this repository and MIT-licensed
with it.
Licensed wallpapers may be added back one at a time; each needs its source and
licence on its line here, and anything still marked UNAUDITED fails
bin/oal-dev-notice-check --strict. (List generated by that command's --update.)

